# Line-coverage floor (percent of lines) for scripts/coverage.sh, one line
# per coverage tool, because llvm-cov and gcov count lines differently.
# The script fails below the floor and prints the value to record when the
# total has risen by a whole percent; raise the floor in the same change.
# Values are whole percent, rounded down from the measured total.
#
# llvm-cov: measured 33.21% with Apple clang 21 on macOS arm64 (TASK29),
# from an empty build/coverage (the script cleans it on every run).
# Re-measured after the client parser tests (TASK66): 33.71% of 18771 lines;
# that total now includes six client files (cl_download, cl_entities,
# cl_network, cl_parse, cl_screen, sound/sound.c), so a loss under
# src/common or src/server can be offset by client lines.
# gcov: NOT measured. TASK29 was written on a host without gcc, and the
# Linux CI job only runs on a pull request. 25 is a conservative lower
# bound chosen below the llvm-cov measurement (gcov counts lines a little
# differently, but not by eight points). The first Linux CI run measures
# it: the "Coverage" step of .github/workflows/linux_x86_64.yml prints
# "TOTAL NN.NN% of N lines" and, when that is a whole percent or more
# above this floor, "set the 'gcov' line in scripts/coverage-floor to N".
# Raise the line below to that N then.
llvm-cov 33
gcov 25
